The argument parsing logic for `--title`, `--body`, `--label`, and `--tier` is repetitive and should be refactored for robustness. Use a method that consistently handles both `--flag=value` and `--flag value` formats, ensuring that flags requiring arguments are processed correctly. This aligns with the repository's requirement to use a robust method for extracting specific arguments from CLI strings by accounting for different flag formats and maintaining a whitelist of flags that consume additional arguments.

```suggestion
		--title=*) title="${option#*=}"; shift ;;
		--title) [[ $# -lt 2 ]] && { log_error "--title requires a value"; return 1; }; title="$2"; shift 2 ;;
		--body=*) body="${option#*=}"; shift ;;
		--body) [[ $# -lt 2 ]] && { log_error "--body requires a value"; return 1; }; body="$2"; shift 2 ;;
		--label=*) label="${option#*=}"; shift ;;
		--label) [[ $# -lt 2 ]] && { log_error "--label requires a value"; return 1; }; label="$2"; shift 2 ;;
		--auto-dispatch) auto_dispatch="yes"; shift ;;
		--tier=*) tier="${option#*=}"; shift ;;
		--tier) [[ $# -lt 2 ]] && { log_error "--tier requires a value"; return 1; }; tier="$2"; shift 2 ;;
```

